1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:56,954
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00:57,224 --> 00:00:58,384
Dip it in the sauce.

3
00:00:58,384 --> 00:00:59,700
That's how it's good.

4
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:02,048
I'll eat it my way.

5
00:01:02,048 --> 00:01:03,449
I'm telling you, this is how you eat it.

6
00:01:03,449 --> 00:01:04,476
Come on!

7
00:01:04,476 --> 00:01:07,528
Hey, trust me and try it.

8
00:01:07,528 --> 00:01:09,180
Jeez.

9
00:01:09,180 --> 00:01:11,736
I like the natural taste of tuna rice balls.

10
00:01:11,736 --> 00:01:13,216
Natural taste, my foot.

11
00:01:13,216 --> 00:01:15,149
This is the way to eat tteokbokki.

12
00:01:15,149 --> 00:01:17,284
You can dip the fried rice in the sauce later.

13
00:01:17,284 --> 00:01:21,380
You've gotta eat the fried rice as is, nice and crispy.

14
00:01:21,380 --> 00:01:23,716
Jeez, we just don't agree on anything.

15
00:01:23,716 --> 00:01:25,983
- Bring me some more pickled radish. - Sure.

16
00:01:30,383 --> 00:01:32,249
Oh, gosh. Another drink?

17
00:01:36,472 --> 00:01:38,172
It's Yoo Ji Hyun.

18
00:01:39,404 --> 00:01:43,249
I reviewed the contract for the Laknes ad.

19
00:01:43,249 --> 00:01:45,628
So I kind of feel closer to her now.

20
00:01:45,628 --> 00:01:48,860
I feel the same. Now that she's our model, I like her even more.

21
00:01:48,860 --> 00:01:50,268
Right?

22
00:01:50,268 --> 00:01:53,156
Jeez, I wish things had gone well for her.

23
00:01:53,156 --> 00:01:54,680
Why'd she have to get divorced?

24
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:58,292
She lost her marriage and her modeling money.

25
00:01:58,292 --> 00:02:00,224
Why her modeling money?

26
00:02:00,224 --> 00:02:02,756
In a situation like this, they usually terminate the contract.

27
00:02:02,756 --> 00:02:04,816
The ad hasn't even aired yet,

28
00:02:04,816 --> 00:02:08,349
so the company has no reason to use someone who's become controversial.

29
00:02:09,396 --> 00:02:11,096
Jeez.

30
00:02:17,016 --> 00:02:22,183
[Episode 6, The Problem of Recognizing Problems]

31
00:02:25,640 --> 00:02:27,449
Alright, alright.

32
00:02:29,848 --> 00:02:31,096
Hazelnut?

33
00:02:31,096 --> 00:02:32,416
Of course.

34
00:02:32,416 --> 00:02:33,683
You haven't forgotten, huh?

35
00:02:33,683 --> 00:02:36,616
How could I forget your favorite, Team Leader?

36
00:02:39,288 --> 00:02:41,216
So what did you want to talk about?

37
00:02:41,216 --> 00:02:42,816
Talk about?

38
00:02:42,816 --> 00:02:46,783
I just wanted to grab coffee and catch up since it's been a while.

39
00:02:46,783 --> 00:02:48,783
Cut the crap.

40
00:02:50,449 --> 00:02:53,349
Well, I mean that contract worker.

41
00:02:53,349 --> 00:02:54,649
What about the contract worker?

42
00:02:54,649 --> 00:02:57,916
Oh, I noticed the contract worker on Team 2 is doing a great job.

43
00:02:57,916 --> 00:03:00,432
Yeah, she's good.

44
00:03:00,432 --> 00:03:04,316
Since the Team 2 girl is doing well, you don't need to worry about her.

45
00:03:04,316 --> 00:03:09,783
But could you keep an eye on our Team 5's Lee Ji Hye?

46
00:03:17,684 --> 00:03:20,700
Do you know what people at the company think of you?

47
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:22,980
- My reputation, all of a sudden? - Yeah.

48
00:03:22,980 --> 00:03:24,149
What do they think?

49
00:03:24,149 --> 00:03:27,388
Your reviews are good. They call you an ace.

50
00:03:27,388 --> 00:03:29,549
Oh, that's all thanks to

51
00:03:29,549 --> 00:03:30,872
- what you taught me... - But

52
00:03:30,872 --> 00:03:33,749
why do you think you're still an assistant manager?

53
00:03:36,649 --> 00:03:39,883
I'll take whatever you say to heart.

54
00:03:40,688 --> 00:03:42,652
You're good at solving problems.

55
00:03:42,652 --> 00:03:46,016
But they're mostly problems within the company.

56
00:03:46,016 --> 00:03:49,220
Your boss' demands, managing your juniors,

57
00:03:49,220 --> 00:03:51,364
office politics, things like that.

58
00:03:51,364 --> 00:03:55,480
So it makes people wonder if you can solve the company's

59
00:03:55,480 --> 00:03:57,516
real big problems.

60
00:03:59,148 --> 00:04:01,302
I'm telling you this because I care about you,

61
00:04:01,302 --> 00:04:02,449
so don't take it the wrong way.

62
00:04:02,449 --> 00:04:06,049
Oh, not at all, sir. I'm not hurt.

63
00:04:06,049 --> 00:04:09,416
So stop worrying about contract workers

64
00:04:09,416 --> 00:04:11,112
and focus on doing some real work.

65
00:04:11,112 --> 00:04:12,992
It will be better for you.

66
00:04:12,992 --> 00:04:14,692
Yes, sir.

67
00:04:19,200 --> 00:04:20,836
By the way,

68
00:04:20,836 --> 00:04:23,044
your team's contract worker is Lee Ji Hye,

69
00:04:23,044 --> 00:04:25,683
but ours is just "the contract worker"?

70
00:04:26,576 --> 00:04:30,883
You don't even know my team member's name, yet you are asking me for a favor?

71
00:04:31,652 --> 00:04:33,500
Yoon Jung Min.

72
00:04:33,500 --> 00:04:35,624
That's the contract worker on my team.

73
00:04:35,624 --> 00:04:37,324
Okay.

74
00:04:39,183 --> 00:04:40,983
Excuse me.

75
00:04:43,672 --> 00:04:45,849
Yes, hello.

76
00:04:46,649 --> 00:04:48,349
Yeah.

77
00:04:49,060 --> 00:04:50,783
Pardon?

78
00:04:59,676 --> 00:05:02,204
- You're here. - Yes, you're back.

79
00:05:02,204 --> 00:05:03,252
Where is Gi Tae?

80
00:05:03,252 --> 00:05:06,183
Gi Tae hasn't come in yet.

81
00:05:15,216 --> 00:05:17,912
[Assistant Manager Yang Jun Ho]

82
00:05:17,912 --> 00:05:19,896
Yes, I understand what you're saying.

83
00:05:19,896 --> 00:05:21,868
I'm sorry we were slow to respond.

84
00:05:21,868 --> 00:05:23,616
Yes, goodbye.

85
00:05:25,176 --> 00:05:26,896
The logistics team is in chaos, right?

86
00:05:26,896 --> 00:05:29,549
Yes, they're pretty upset because the schedule got messed up.

87
00:05:29,549 --> 00:05:30,549
Can't you reach Gi Tae?

88
00:05:30,549 --> 00:05:31,549
[Park Gi Tae]

89
00:05:31,549 --> 00:05:32,983
He isn't answering.

90
00:05:32,983 --> 00:05:37,216
Gi Tae wouldn't bail just because he screwed up, would he?

91
00:05:38,316 --> 00:05:40,268
Let's focus on getting this fixed.

92
00:05:40,268 --> 00:05:42,283
Alright, to sum things up,

93
00:05:42,283 --> 00:05:44,408
we placed an additional order for 300 million won,

94
00:05:44,408 --> 00:05:46,952
but the purchase order listed three billion.

95
00:05:46,952 --> 00:05:49,480
Laknes shipped the amount on the purchase order,

96
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:51,952
and the shipment has arrived in Incheon, right?

97
00:05:51,952 --> 00:05:55,308
But Laknes didn't say anything about it?

98
00:05:55,308 --> 00:05:58,916
They must've known there was a problem with the order quantity.

99
00:05:58,916 --> 00:06:00,360
We can't know that for sure.

100
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:02,028
Let's not jump to conclusions.

101
00:06:02,028 --> 00:06:06,884
Even 300 million won was more than enough. Three billion is impossible to move.

102
00:06:06,884 --> 00:06:09,548
Wouldn't that be over ten billion won at retail prices?

103
00:06:09,548 --> 00:06:10,876
So we know what the problem is.

104
00:06:10,876 --> 00:06:12,816
How do we fix it?

105
00:06:15,436 --> 00:06:17,388
First, we need to deal with Gi Tae not showing up.

106
00:06:17,388 --> 00:06:19,132
I'll report to Deputy Director Jang first.

107
00:06:19,132 --> 00:06:21,460
Ms. Jang, come with me to the report.

108
00:06:21,460 --> 00:06:26,032
Mr. Yang and Ji Hye, please find Gi Tae and bring him to me.

109
00:06:26,032 --> 00:06:29,916
Mr. Gong, can't I go with you for the report?

110
00:06:33,249 --> 00:06:36,708
I only suggested it because you're close with Gi Tae.

111
00:06:36,708 --> 00:06:38,849
Well, we're close,

112
00:06:38,849 --> 00:06:40,849
- but in a situation like this... - Then I'll go.

113
00:06:40,849 --> 00:06:42,583
It's fine.

114
00:06:45,852 --> 00:06:48,349
- Alright then. - Okay.

115
00:06:51,964 --> 00:06:53,472
He's inside, right?

116
00:06:53,472 --> 00:06:55,172
Yes.

117
00:06:57,856 --> 00:06:59,556
Come in.

118
00:07:05,688 --> 00:07:07,508
Where is Park Gi Tae?

119
00:07:07,508 --> 00:07:09,416
They're out looking for him.

120
00:07:11,352 --> 00:07:14,649
Isn't the purchase order your responsibility? Didn't you check it?

121
00:07:15,832 --> 00:07:18,092
The original request was 250 million won.

122
00:07:18,092 --> 00:07:21,108
I revised it to 300 million after checking,

123
00:07:21,108 --> 00:07:23,183
but I didn't properly check it after that.

124
00:07:23,183 --> 00:07:24,916
Are you seriously bragging right now?

125
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:27,460
I'm sorry.

126
00:07:28,436 --> 00:07:32,216
Didn't Ms. Park tell you just the other day to report every single won?

127
00:07:34,640 --> 00:07:37,249
You reported it, so let's say you're off the hook.

128
00:07:37,249 --> 00:07:39,283
What about me, huh?

129
00:07:40,040 --> 00:07:41,883
Am I supposed to report this?

130
00:07:43,148 --> 00:07:47,004
Give me three days, and I think I can fix it.

131
00:07:47,004 --> 00:07:52,116
I think we can get the numbers straight before the quarterly report.

132
00:07:53,483 --> 00:07:57,383
"I can do it" and "I think I can do it."

133
00:07:57,383 --> 00:08:01,500
Those two are very different. Which one is it?

134
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:02,616
I think I can do it.

135
00:08:02,616 --> 00:08:04,316
Darn it.

136
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:08,983
Give it a shot.

137
00:08:08,983 --> 00:08:11,276
I'll report it in three days, no matter what.

138
00:08:11,276 --> 00:08:15,549
Whether this gets reported as a minor incident or a major problem

139
00:08:15,549 --> 00:08:17,916
is up to you two.

140
00:08:17,916 --> 00:08:19,616
Yes, sir.

141
00:08:24,668 --> 00:08:27,916
But Jang Hyang Eun went after Park Gi Tae? You didn't go?

142
00:08:27,916 --> 00:08:31,388
Oh, yes. Lee Ji Hye went with her.

143
00:08:31,388 --> 00:08:34,616
Why do something you normally don't? Just stick to what you usually do.

144
00:08:38,016 --> 00:08:40,116
Just solve the problem first.

145
00:08:40,116 --> 00:08:42,404
And bring Park Gi Tae back alive.

146
00:08:42,404 --> 00:08:43,568
Okay.

147
00:08:43,568 --> 00:08:45,383
Do you have a plan?

148
00:08:49,783 --> 00:08:52,483
- I think I do. - You... darn it.

149
00:09:06,076 --> 00:09:07,980
You can get some sleep.

150
00:09:07,980 --> 00:09:10,304
No, I'm fine.

151
00:09:10,304 --> 00:09:13,176
You can relax. Do I make you uncomfortable?

152
00:09:13,176 --> 00:09:15,949
No, not at all.

153
00:09:15,949 --> 00:09:19,424
I just want to show you some respect.

154
00:09:19,424 --> 00:09:22,636
Telling you to relax doesn't mean you can be rude anyway, right?

155
00:09:22,636 --> 00:09:24,336
Yes.

156
00:09:28,616 --> 00:09:31,516
So, how was life in China?

157
00:09:32,656 --> 00:09:34,396
It was boring.

158
00:09:34,396 --> 00:09:36,328
When men get posted abroad,

159
00:09:36,328 --> 00:09:39,880
they usually get wild, while women get bored.

160
00:09:39,880 --> 00:09:41,808
I feel like all I did was work.

161
00:09:41,808 --> 00:09:46,504
Oh, I can see that.

162
00:09:46,504 --> 00:09:48,816
Is that why you came back?

163
00:09:50,149 --> 00:09:52,916
Haven't you heard any rumors about me?

164
00:09:53,820 --> 00:09:55,548
Like what?

165
00:09:55,548 --> 00:09:57,756
That I committed fraud in China and ran.

166
00:09:57,756 --> 00:10:00,540
That I got off easy because I was sleeping with a senior executive.

167
00:10:00,540 --> 00:10:02,468
That I'm dating someone from another team.

168
00:10:02,468 --> 00:10:04,516
That all my clothes are knockoffs.

169
00:10:04,516 --> 00:10:06,383
That you can see me every day at the yellow tents in Dongdaemun.

170
00:10:06,383 --> 00:10:08,916
That I make four million won and spend five million on clothes.

171
00:10:08,916 --> 00:10:13,136
That's all I've heard. You really haven't heard any of it?

172
00:10:13,136 --> 00:10:16,704
No, I've never heard any of it.

173
00:10:16,704 --> 00:10:22,312
All I've heard from our team is that you're an incredible ace.

174
00:10:22,312 --> 00:10:25,716
If it weren't for our team, I might've quit.

175
00:10:25,716 --> 00:10:27,349
If I'd been on another team,

176
00:10:27,349 --> 00:10:30,349
they'd probably have grilled me about whether the rumors were true

177
00:10:30,349 --> 00:10:32,449
and what happened in China.

178
00:10:33,316 --> 00:10:37,196
Shouldn't you do something instead of just putting up with it?

179
00:10:37,196 --> 00:10:39,716
Of course, I want to do something.

180
00:10:39,716 --> 00:10:42,268
But I just don't know how.

181
00:10:42,268 --> 00:10:46,112
You can't explain away things people say behind your back.

182
00:10:46,112 --> 00:10:49,304
People will believe it if they want to and won't if they don't.

183
00:10:49,304 --> 00:10:51,716
I just have to hope there are more of the latter.

184
00:10:57,180 --> 00:11:01,449
But do you really think Laknes didn't know it was a mistake?

185
00:11:01,449 --> 00:11:03,716
You know they did. There's no way they didn't.

186
00:11:04,864 --> 00:11:09,264
I mean, even if we admit it was our mistake, it's still really frustrating.

187
00:11:09,264 --> 00:11:10,516
Well, what can we do?

188
00:11:10,516 --> 00:11:14,135
It's a world where one mistake gets you torn apart.

189
00:11:14,135 --> 00:11:18,816
Simply put, we just need to expand our sales channels.

190
00:11:18,816 --> 00:11:22,483
But sales channels don't just fall from the sky.

191
00:11:23,383 --> 00:11:25,416
Actually, there is one.

192
00:11:26,584 --> 00:11:28,952
So, Mr. Gong,

193
00:11:28,952 --> 00:11:32,649
we need to make sure the additional order wasn't our mistake.

194
00:11:44,424 --> 00:11:45,883
[Join]

195
00:11:46,672 --> 00:11:48,583
Hello, Mr. Gong.

196
00:11:48,583 --> 00:11:51,200
Yes, hello, Director.

197
00:11:51,200 --> 00:11:54,049
We checked after your sudden conference request,

198
00:11:54,049 --> 00:11:56,716
and the additional order was much larger than expected.

199
00:11:56,716 --> 00:11:59,932
Yes, it'd have been great if you had confirmed it with us.

200
00:11:59,932 --> 00:12:01,676
I regret that as well.

201
00:12:01,676 --> 00:12:03,616
I think the person in charge

202
00:12:03,616 --> 00:12:06,376
may have thought it was the regular order, not an additional one.

203
00:12:06,376 --> 00:12:09,704
Yes. Since it's been two months since the last regular order,

204
00:12:09,704 --> 00:12:12,944
I suppose they thought they were simply receiving the regular order a little early.

205
00:12:12,944 --> 00:12:15,936
Well, it's not our mistake,

206
00:12:15,936 --> 00:12:18,908
but let's see if we can work this out together.

207
00:12:18,908 --> 00:12:21,116
Well, actually, about that,

208
00:12:21,116 --> 00:12:23,116
it wasn't a mistake.

209
00:12:24,352 --> 00:12:26,404
Where else can we sell them?

210
00:12:26,404 --> 00:12:28,749
We have our select shop.

211
00:12:29,716 --> 00:12:31,983
You're saying it wasn't a mistake?

212
00:12:31,983 --> 00:12:35,484
Then I think you owe me an explanation.

213
00:12:35,484 --> 00:12:38,948
Yes. It was a last-minute decision, so I couldn't tell you in advance,

214
00:12:38,948 --> 00:12:43,420
but we're planning to carry Laknes at the shoe boutique we're launching.

215
00:12:43,420 --> 00:12:46,083
Oh, I see.

216
00:12:46,083 --> 00:12:49,624
So that's why you placed such a large order?

217
00:12:49,624 --> 00:12:53,308
Yes, we were supposed to reorder after negotiating the invoice price,

218
00:12:53,308 --> 00:12:55,612
but there was a mix-up.

219
00:12:55,612 --> 00:12:57,816
You're renegotiating the price?

220
00:12:57,816 --> 00:13:00,344
Yes. The order quantity has increased significantly,

221
00:13:00,344 --> 00:13:02,716
so the price should be adjusted.

222
00:13:03,528 --> 00:13:05,228
By how much?

223
00:13:05,849 --> 00:13:07,649
Enough to justify it.

224
00:13:07,649 --> 00:13:11,749
There's actually some opposition to Laknes joining the select shop.

225
00:13:11,749 --> 00:13:13,583
Other brands are also

226
00:13:13,583 --> 00:13:17,783
pushing back against having to sell Laknes shoes alongside their own.

227
00:13:17,783 --> 00:13:21,283
Oh, I'm very sorry that we got the order of things wrong.

228
00:13:21,283 --> 00:13:26,064
We'd appreciate it if Laknes could give us some justification.

229
00:13:26,064 --> 00:13:28,880
What is the scale of this select shop?

230
00:13:28,880 --> 00:13:31,260
We're opening 40 locations at once.

231
00:13:31,260 --> 00:13:32,960
40...

232
00:13:37,749 --> 00:13:39,816
If we adjust the additional volume's total

233
00:13:40,516 --> 00:13:43,183
to 2 billion won, would that work?

234
00:13:45,888 --> 00:13:50,080
Yes, I think that's a fair price. And that should give us enough justification.

235
00:13:50,080 --> 00:13:55,016
However, could you do 1.5 billion won for this order only?

236
00:13:55,749 --> 00:13:57,416
1.5 billion?

237
00:13:57,416 --> 00:13:58,700
Do you think that will work?

238
00:13:58,700 --> 00:14:03,596
If they sent it knowing it was our mess-up, they might feel a little guilty.

239
00:14:03,596 --> 00:14:06,149
Then it might work.

240
00:14:06,149 --> 00:14:08,949
Yes, this shoe boutique

241
00:14:08,949 --> 00:14:11,649
is a company-wide initiative.

242
00:14:11,649 --> 00:14:14,183
It would mean a lot to us

243
00:14:14,183 --> 00:14:17,316
if Laknes could help us out this time.

244
00:14:17,316 --> 00:14:19,004
And it'll be a reminder

245
00:14:19,004 --> 00:14:22,183
for both of us not to make mistakes like this again.

246
00:14:42,883 --> 00:14:44,052
Alright.

247
00:14:44,052 --> 00:14:46,016
We'll do it this time.

248
00:14:49,283 --> 00:14:50,583
Thank you.

249
00:14:50,583 --> 00:14:53,349
Not at all. It's a good opportunity for us too.

250
00:14:53,349 --> 00:14:55,583
I hope it works out well for you.

251
00:14:55,583 --> 00:14:58,680
And if you don't mind, how about

252
00:14:58,680 --> 00:15:02,124
we include some Laknes shopping bags at the select shop?

253
00:15:02,124 --> 00:15:04,916
For promotional purposes.

254
00:15:04,916 --> 00:15:07,336
- Sure, why not? - Then we'll expect you to send them over

255
00:15:07,336 --> 00:15:09,283
and proceed accordingly.

256
00:15:09,283 --> 00:15:11,483
- Thank you. - Sure.

257
00:15:12,516 --> 00:15:14,556
[Call Ended]

258
00:15:14,556 --> 00:15:18,749
Those shopping bags alone could add up to ten million won.

259
00:15:19,992 --> 00:15:21,383
What?

260
00:15:21,383 --> 00:15:23,116
You are amazing.

261
00:15:29,392 --> 00:15:33,749
Do you really think they ordered them for the select shops?

262
00:15:34,592 --> 00:15:38,783
You know that's ridiculous.

263
00:15:50,164 --> 00:15:53,349
Chief, Chief, Chief!

264
00:15:53,349 --> 00:15:56,049
Here, I got the documents.

265
00:15:56,776 --> 00:15:58,349
You got them from the Port Authority?

266
00:15:58,349 --> 00:16:00,049
Yes.

267
00:16:01,449 --> 00:16:02,549
[Report on Port Stevedoring Tariffs and Fees (Revision)]

268
00:16:02,549 --> 00:16:04,149
Wait, they actually approved this?

269
00:16:04,149 --> 00:16:07,364
This grants permission for two weeks of free storage after unloading.

270
00:16:07,364 --> 00:16:09,664
So we're all set now?

271
00:16:09,664 --> 00:16:12,520
Yeah, well, you've got two weeks, okay?

272
00:16:12,520 --> 00:16:14,916
After that, you're on your own. Got it?

273
00:16:15,860 --> 00:16:17,783
Thank you so much, thank you so much!

274
00:16:17,783 --> 00:16:20,480
Oh, take that phone with you.

275
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:22,192
It's been ringing all day.

276
00:16:22,192 --> 00:16:23,983
Oh, okay.

277
00:16:26,583 --> 00:16:29,216
[Missed Call, Assistant Manager Yang Jun Ho] Jeez.

278
00:16:30,916 --> 00:16:33,583
Thank you, thank you!

279
00:16:37,400 --> 00:16:40,383
Ji Hye... Ms. Jang...

280
00:16:50,004 --> 00:16:54,916
So you were trying to fix it before reporting it?

281
00:16:54,916 --> 00:16:58,683
Yes. I thought it was the least I could do.

282
00:17:00,912 --> 00:17:03,160
What is going to happen to us?

283
00:17:03,160 --> 00:17:04,608
Why do you ask?

284
00:17:04,608 --> 00:17:07,332
Do you think you'll get fired over one mistake?

285
00:17:07,332 --> 00:17:10,149
Well, I don't care about getting fired, but...

286
00:17:10,149 --> 00:17:12,883
won't this affect the team's performance?

287
00:17:14,220 --> 00:17:17,283
Ugh, and it might reflect badly on Ji Hye too.

288
00:17:18,152 --> 00:17:22,049
Gi Tae, why would you think that?

289
00:17:25,744 --> 00:17:29,883
Mr. Gong told me to pass a message to you when we found you.

290
00:17:29,883 --> 00:17:32,416
- Ms. Jang? - Yes.

291
00:17:32,416 --> 00:17:34,856
Go check the port authority or the container terminal.

292
00:17:34,856 --> 00:17:38,848
Gi Tae isn't the type to hide somewhere and drown his sorrows in booze.

293
00:17:38,848 --> 00:17:41,749
- Okay. - And make sure you tell him this.

294
00:17:44,688 --> 00:17:47,248
This incident is my responsibility,

295
00:17:47,248 --> 00:17:49,108
and I'll take responsibility for it.

296
00:17:49,108 --> 00:17:53,484
"This incident is my responsibility, and I'll take responsibility for it."

297
00:17:53,484 --> 00:17:56,500
"Don't get cocky and try to take the blame yourself."

298
00:17:56,500 --> 00:17:58,200
That's what he said.

299
00:17:59,784 --> 00:18:01,940
That doesn't sound like him.

300
00:18:01,940 --> 00:18:04,016
The sentiment is the same.

301
00:18:07,324 --> 00:18:10,588
Don't you think Mr. Gong will be upset?

302
00:18:10,588 --> 00:18:11,628
Because I caused the mess?

303
00:18:11,628 --> 00:18:14,200
No. Because you didn't report it.

304
00:18:14,200 --> 00:18:18,104
After Mr. Gong found out, the first thing he did was report it to Mr. Jang.

305
00:18:18,104 --> 00:18:20,664
Because he trusts Mr. Jang.

306
00:18:20,664 --> 00:18:22,080
Right now, you're treating him

307
00:18:22,080 --> 00:18:26,116
like someone who passes the buck and can't handle things.

308
00:18:27,476 --> 00:18:30,536
Do you really think he'd see it that way?

309
00:18:30,536 --> 00:18:32,076
I'm sure he wouldn't.

310
00:18:32,076 --> 00:18:34,416
Oh, okay.

311
00:18:34,416 --> 00:18:38,268
Look, everyone who works has messed up at some point.

312
00:18:38,268 --> 00:18:41,648
So I'm saying don't make such a big deal out of it. Got it?

313
00:18:41,648 --> 00:18:44,849
Does everyone make mistakes this big?

314
00:18:44,849 --> 00:18:46,696
Usually not this huge, no.

315
00:18:46,696 --> 00:18:49,116
Oh, okay.

316
00:19:03,116 --> 00:19:06,483
[Advertising Appearance Agreement]

317
00:19:09,756 --> 00:19:11,336
How urgent is it?

318
00:19:11,336 --> 00:19:15,683
Oh, they've taken the contract, so we need it within an hour.

319
00:19:15,683 --> 00:19:18,488
They already took the contract?

320
00:19:18,488 --> 00:19:20,164
Are you kidding me?

321
00:19:20,164 --> 00:19:22,504
I know it's asking a lot.

322
00:19:22,504 --> 00:19:25,016
We've already covered half the loss,

323
00:19:25,016 --> 00:19:26,916
so I think we can somehow manage with just this.

324
00:19:26,916 --> 00:19:30,580
Even so, how can we do a legal review in an hour?

325
00:19:30,580 --> 00:19:34,264
You're calling it a review, but you're actually asking me to approve it, huh?

326
00:19:34,264 --> 00:19:36,983
We can't afford to miss the timing.

327
00:19:38,444 --> 00:19:41,283
Then you should've brought me a normal contract.

328
00:19:41,283 --> 00:19:42,528
What is this?

329
00:19:42,528 --> 00:19:47,232
[Article 8: Conduct and Reputation] Why are all these unheard-of clauses in here?

330
00:19:47,232 --> 00:19:49,716
I didn't write them myself, so...

331
00:19:52,292 --> 00:19:53,848
I know you're in a hurry,

332
00:19:53,848 --> 00:19:56,704
but we have procedures and accountability to consider.

333
00:19:56,704 --> 00:19:57,908
If I approve a contract like this,

334
00:19:57,908 --> 00:20:00,232
I'll have to explain why I approved it.

335
00:20:00,232 --> 00:20:01,583
I know that all too well.

336
00:20:01,583 --> 00:20:03,028
That's why I'm asking you.

337
00:20:03,028 --> 00:20:05,084
I'm not asking without understanding the risks.

338
00:20:07,016 --> 00:20:10,783
From the team leader down to the team members, seriously.

339
00:21:05,216 --> 00:21:07,228
Are you from Hongsung?

340
00:21:07,228 --> 00:21:08,983
Yes.

341
00:21:11,456 --> 00:21:13,149
Please have a seat.

342
00:21:13,149 --> 00:21:15,483
[Gong Eun Tae]

343
00:21:15,483 --> 00:21:18,283
[Hongsung International]

344
00:21:19,449 --> 00:21:21,948
Thanks for coming all this way.

345
00:21:21,948 --> 00:21:23,468
Not at all.

346
00:21:23,468 --> 00:21:26,749
The weather's nice, so it felt like a picnic.

347
00:21:28,783 --> 00:21:31,608
I see you're into woodworking.

348
00:21:31,608 --> 00:21:35,652
Our work can feel a little empty sometimes.

349
00:21:35,652 --> 00:21:37,728
Like it's all an illusion.

350
00:21:37,728 --> 00:21:40,352
Making something with my hands

351
00:21:40,352 --> 00:21:44,064
seems to help me stay sane.

352
00:21:44,064 --> 00:21:47,244
Plus, I don't really have any other hobbies.

353
00:21:47,244 --> 00:21:49,300
That's about it.

354
00:21:49,300 --> 00:21:50,916
It looks great, though.

355
00:21:50,916 --> 00:21:54,116
Most people who have a hobby make something by writing,

356
00:21:54,116 --> 00:21:56,216
but you're actually making something, right?

357
00:21:57,376 --> 00:22:01,868
So what are you planning to do?

358
00:22:01,868 --> 00:22:02,948
Oh, yes.

359
00:22:02,948 --> 00:22:05,680
I'm not good at beating around the bush.

360
00:22:05,680 --> 00:22:08,816
That was my best effort at small talk.

361
00:22:08,816 --> 00:22:12,816
It probably isn't good news, so let's get it over with.

362
00:22:14,324 --> 00:22:17,183
Why do you think it's bad news?

363
00:22:18,428 --> 00:22:21,580
Aren't you here to terminate my modeling contract?

364
00:22:21,580 --> 00:22:25,336
You don't need a divorced actress

365
00:22:25,336 --> 00:22:27,983
as the face of a brand you're launching.

366
00:22:29,100 --> 00:22:32,249
I'm sorry I couldn't tell you

367
00:22:32,249 --> 00:22:33,983
before the contract.

368
00:22:34,596 --> 00:22:37,292
Couples break up and make up all the time.

369
00:22:37,292 --> 00:22:40,349
And stay together only to split again.

370
00:22:41,436 --> 00:22:44,116
I wasn't certain about the divorce back then. Well...

371
00:22:45,124 --> 00:22:47,016
It's not really a flaw, anyway.

372
00:22:49,436 --> 00:22:52,104
We have no intention of terminating the contract.

373
00:22:52,104 --> 00:22:55,449
I came to ask you for a favor.

374
00:22:56,584 --> 00:22:58,284
What is it?

375
00:22:59,536 --> 00:23:02,116
One moment please. It's an important text.

376
00:23:02,916 --> 00:23:06,449
[Review complete. You may hand over the contract]

377
00:23:07,304 --> 00:23:09,004
Sorry about that.

378
00:23:12,016 --> 00:23:14,316
We're planning to draw up a new contract.

379
00:23:15,276 --> 00:23:18,048
I'd like you to look over the contract first.

380
00:23:18,048 --> 00:23:21,148
Paperwork gives me a headache right now.

381
00:23:21,148 --> 00:23:23,140
Can I have my lawyer review it and get back to you?

382
00:23:23,140 --> 00:23:24,220
Yes, that's fine.

383
00:23:24,220 --> 00:23:27,883
But I'd appreciate it if you could just confirm Article 8 first.

384
00:23:30,328 --> 00:23:32,249
What is in Article 8?

385
00:23:32,900 --> 00:23:34,716
We revised the morality clause.

386
00:23:34,716 --> 00:23:36,416
[Article 8: Conduct and Reputation]

387
00:23:37,196 --> 00:23:38,516
As you can see,

388
00:23:38,516 --> 00:23:42,812
we made the morality clause apply to both sides in this contract.

389
00:23:42,812 --> 00:23:47,772
It's usually there to cover cases where a model causes a public scandal,

390
00:23:47,772 --> 00:23:51,616
but brands can also cause harm to their models.

391
00:23:51,616 --> 00:23:54,783
However, since we're the ones paying you,

392
00:23:54,783 --> 00:23:56,868
the penalties aren't equal.

393
00:23:56,868 --> 00:23:59,372
I hope you can understand that.

394
00:23:59,372 --> 00:24:02,649
The morality clause applies to both parties?

395
00:24:04,360 --> 00:24:05,688
Is that allowed?

396
00:24:05,688 --> 00:24:09,260
Your divorce is not a public scandal, Ms. Yoo.

397
00:24:09,260 --> 00:24:10,712
If you have to worry about losing your contract

398
00:24:10,712 --> 00:24:12,116
simply because you're getting divorced,

399
00:24:12,116 --> 00:24:16,480
I believe that's clearly unfair, so we changed the wording.

400
00:24:16,480 --> 00:24:20,572
So I'd like to confirm one thing.

401
00:24:20,572 --> 00:24:22,449
Are you responsible

402
00:24:23,228 --> 00:24:25,449
for this divorce?

403
00:24:28,672 --> 00:24:32,144
Both sides are responsible, I suppose. But...

404
00:24:32,144 --> 00:24:34,848
As for the wrongdoing you're referring to,

405
00:24:34,848 --> 00:24:36,683
I didn't do anything wrong.

406
00:24:38,204 --> 00:24:41,049
That's enough. Then let's sign the contract.

407
00:24:45,048 --> 00:24:47,620
You could've terminated my contract,

408
00:24:47,620 --> 00:24:50,928
yet you came with an even better one.

409
00:24:50,928 --> 00:24:53,483
So what can I do for you in return?

410
00:24:54,392 --> 00:24:56,916
Please appear in court for the divorce hearing.

411
00:24:58,436 --> 00:25:00,976
Should I wear Laknes shoes?

412
00:25:00,976 --> 00:25:02,676
Yes.

413
00:25:09,404 --> 00:25:11,524
You're something else.

414
00:25:11,524 --> 00:25:13,624
I know it's a big favor.

415
00:25:13,624 --> 00:25:16,283
That's why you revised the contract too?

416
00:25:23,516 --> 00:25:25,260
I'll do it.

417
00:25:25,260 --> 00:25:30,349
I know how difficult it is to get a contract like this approved.

418
00:25:31,048 --> 00:25:32,783
Thank you.

419
00:25:35,983 --> 00:25:37,716
Mr. Gong,

420
00:25:37,716 --> 00:25:40,216
would you consider being my manager?

421
00:25:42,032 --> 00:25:43,404
I'm serious.

422
00:25:43,404 --> 00:25:45,683
I'll pay you more than you're making now.

423
00:25:48,376 --> 00:25:50,816
Are you considering it right now?

424
00:25:50,816 --> 00:25:52,556
No,

425
00:25:52,556 --> 00:25:55,116
I was just trying to think of a polite way to say no.

426
00:25:55,116 --> 00:25:59,283
Just say it. I was rude too.

427
00:26:00,160 --> 00:26:02,424
I'm sorry,

428
00:26:02,424 --> 00:26:04,416
but I have plenty of money myself.

429
00:26:08,583 --> 00:26:11,449
[Seoul Family Court]

430
00:27:55,149 --> 00:27:57,749
[Wow, she made it look like a photoshoot #YooJiHyun #Divorce #CourtFashion]

431
00:27:57,749 --> 00:27:59,316
[Where are those shoes from?]

432
00:27:59,316 --> 00:28:00,349
[Looks like the new Laknes release]

433
00:28:00,349 --> 00:28:02,283
[I already bought a pair]

434
00:28:06,649 --> 00:28:09,383
[She's stunning, I'm speechless #YooJiHyun #IsThisCourt? #Goddess]

435
00:28:09,383 --> 00:28:12,349
[Please share the shoe info]

436
00:28:12,349 --> 00:28:14,249
[I'm off to score some Laknes shoes today]

437
00:28:14,249 --> 00:28:16,416
[Laknes]

438
00:28:16,416 --> 00:28:17,683
[Black Mary Jane Heel Pumps]

439
00:28:17,683 --> 00:28:18,716
[Buy Now]

440
00:28:18,716 --> 00:28:20,449
[Payment Complete]

441
00:29:05,849 --> 00:29:08,216
[Outlet, department store, offline, online, total]

442
00:29:08,916 --> 00:29:10,083
[August Total, September Total]

443
00:29:10,083 --> 00:29:11,949
[Change in Amount, Change Rate]

444
00:29:11,949 --> 00:29:14,316
[September Total, Change in Amount, Change Rate]

445
00:29:18,616 --> 00:29:23,188
I've never seen sales grow 1,400% month-over-month in all my years working.

446
00:29:23,188 --> 00:29:25,300
- Me neither. - Me neither.

447
00:29:25,300 --> 00:29:28,949
Wait, could it be someone added an extra zero like I did?

448
00:29:28,949 --> 00:29:30,452
Jeez!

449
00:29:30,452 --> 00:29:32,212
Let me.

450
00:29:32,212 --> 00:29:34,284
- Ji Hye, you hit him too. - Oh, no. I'm fine.

451
00:29:34,284 --> 00:29:35,983
Come on, you've been through a lot.

452
00:29:35,983 --> 00:29:37,252
Don't regret it later.

453
00:29:37,252 --> 00:29:38,549
Yeah, it's fine. Ji Hye, give me one.

454
00:29:38,549 --> 00:29:40,512
- Ouch! - Oh! Oh, no!

455
00:29:40,512 --> 00:29:42,776
What do you mean, "oh no"? We should stop messing around and get to work.

456
00:29:42,776 --> 00:29:45,783
Oh, Mr. Gong. I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

457
00:29:45,783 --> 00:29:47,116
- Should we, Mr. Gong? - 1,400%.

458
00:29:47,116 --> 00:29:49,040
- Seriously, because of you... - I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

459
00:29:49,040 --> 00:29:50,883
- Seriously... - What are you doing?

460
00:29:52,628 --> 00:29:54,468
I'm sorry, sir.

461
00:29:54,468 --> 00:29:56,168
You, come with me.

462
00:29:59,044 --> 00:30:00,508
The executive director?

463
00:30:00,508 --> 00:30:02,504
Why all of a sudden?

464
00:30:02,504 --> 00:30:04,572
I don't know either.

465
00:30:04,572 --> 00:30:07,836
I just reported the sales growth exactly as it was.

466
00:30:07,836 --> 00:30:11,683
He immediately summoned Ms. Park. And that was 30 minutes ago.

467
00:30:12,296 --> 00:30:14,683
Do you think he's going to reprimand me?

468
00:30:17,288 --> 00:30:19,256
It wouldn't be strange if he reprimanded you,

469
00:30:19,256 --> 00:30:22,483
nor would it be strange if he praised you.

470
00:30:22,483 --> 00:30:24,280
What do you think it'll be?

471
00:30:24,280 --> 00:30:28,644
If he reprimands me, I'll take it calmly.

472
00:30:28,644 --> 00:30:31,583
And if he praises me, I'll accept it humbly.

473
00:30:32,620 --> 00:30:35,016
So you don't care either way?

474
00:30:35,016 --> 00:30:38,049
How he chooses to evaluate me is up to him.

475
00:30:38,049 --> 00:30:42,092
If I were in the same situation again, I'd do the same thing,

476
00:30:42,092 --> 00:30:44,116
so it doesn't really matter.

477
00:30:51,540 --> 00:30:53,240
Why are you looking at me like that?

478
00:30:55,212 --> 00:30:57,449
I have a bad feeling about this.

479
00:31:08,792 --> 00:31:10,492
Come in.

480
00:31:20,424 --> 00:31:22,124
Have a seat.

481
00:31:38,500 --> 00:31:40,200
Mr. Gong,

482
00:31:41,196 --> 00:31:43,049
this is your first time here, right?

483
00:31:44,349 --> 00:31:47,044
Yes, it is my first time.

484
00:31:47,044 --> 00:31:49,083
Why do you think I called you here?

485
00:31:50,336 --> 00:31:51,804
I'm not sure.

486
00:31:51,804 --> 00:31:53,949
You must have some idea.

487
00:31:57,004 --> 00:31:59,849
Sales went up significantly, but since it was caused by a mistake,

488
00:31:59,849 --> 00:32:02,583
I thought you might reprimand me.

489
00:32:03,860 --> 00:32:05,916
I called you here because I'm curious.

490
00:32:07,124 --> 00:32:11,280
You took a brand nobody wanted and made it a success.

491
00:32:11,280 --> 00:32:14,096
I sent you to Italy to deal with a traitor,

492
00:32:14,096 --> 00:32:16,748
and you turned him into an affiliate instead.

493
00:32:16,748 --> 00:32:19,040
The botched order somehow turned

494
00:32:19,040 --> 00:32:22,249
into a brilliant pre-order made in anticipation of a huge success.

495
00:32:22,988 --> 00:32:25,183
At this point, I'm curious.

496
00:32:25,872 --> 00:32:28,612
I've come to two conclusions.

497
00:32:28,612 --> 00:32:31,520
Either your position is too small for your abilities,

498
00:32:31,520 --> 00:32:34,083
or you're overreaching beyond your position.

499
00:32:42,749 --> 00:32:44,583
Try this.

500
00:32:47,964 --> 00:32:50,160
Recently, there was a report about corruption in Sales Team 2.

501
00:32:50,160 --> 00:32:51,180
[Sales Team 2 Audit Plan]

502
00:32:51,180 --> 00:32:52,983
We gave them a light disciplinary action,

503
00:32:52,983 --> 00:32:55,844
but another tip came in right afterward.

504
00:32:55,844 --> 00:32:58,116
It's like finding one cockroach in your house,

505
00:32:58,116 --> 00:33:01,096
plugging the drains and spraying pesticides,

506
00:33:01,096 --> 00:33:03,744
and still getting nowhere.

507
00:33:03,744 --> 00:33:07,040
Because the whole house is already infested.

508
00:33:07,040 --> 00:33:09,576
So the Audit Team has decided to step in.

509
00:33:09,576 --> 00:33:12,749
[Review of Sales Team 2 Transparency] But they lack hands-on experience.

510
00:33:13,416 --> 00:33:15,649
I'd like you to help them.

511
00:33:22,316 --> 00:33:24,352
Well...

512
00:33:24,352 --> 00:33:26,616
With all due respect,

513
00:33:27,449 --> 00:33:32,540
if another sales team audits them, Sales Team 2's backlash will be fierce.

514
00:33:32,540 --> 00:33:34,983
That's why I'm putting you in charge.

515
00:33:35,932 --> 00:33:37,632
Go ahead and stick your neck out.

516
00:33:44,580 --> 00:33:46,449
Think you can handle it?

517
00:33:47,412 --> 00:33:49,508
I'll do my best.

518
00:33:49,508 --> 00:33:51,288
Of course, you'd better.

519
00:33:51,288 --> 00:33:53,716
Doing well is a given.

520
00:33:54,684 --> 00:33:56,516
Keep a straight face.

521
00:33:56,516 --> 00:33:58,328
There's nothing more irritating than an auditor walking around

522
00:33:58,328 --> 00:34:01,288
with a smile on his face.

523
00:34:01,288 --> 00:34:02,988
Yes, ma'am.

524
00:34:04,792 --> 00:34:06,649
I have a bad feeling about this.

525
00:34:21,283 --> 00:34:25,996
If another sales team audits them, Sales Team 2's backlash will be fierce.

526
00:34:25,996 --> 00:34:28,564
That's why I'm putting you in charge.

527
00:34:28,564 --> 00:34:30,264
Go ahead and stick your neck out.

528
00:34:32,316 --> 00:34:35,483
The branch has been involved in some massive corruption.

529
00:34:35,483 --> 00:34:39,660
And there's a rumor she's at the center of it.

530
00:34:39,660 --> 00:34:42,848
You must have a lot of questions for me.

531
00:34:42,848 --> 00:34:44,683
Why didn't you ask?

532
00:35:07,416 --> 00:35:09,116
Over here.

533
00:35:15,683 --> 00:35:18,516
But why did you want to meet outside the office?

534
00:35:19,672 --> 00:35:22,044
I need to talk to you about something in private.

535
00:35:22,044 --> 00:35:23,556
You're making me nervous.

536
00:35:23,556 --> 00:35:27,149
Why would you be nervous? I know you're not that kind of person.

537
00:35:27,149 --> 00:35:29,684
Let me correct that to "concerned."

538
00:35:29,684 --> 00:35:32,583
Try their coffee. It's so good.

539
00:35:38,688 --> 00:35:42,240
I have a favor to ask you.

540
00:35:42,240 --> 00:35:43,649
Sure. What is it?

541
00:35:43,649 --> 00:35:46,932
There's going to be an audit on Sales Team 2.

542
00:35:46,932 --> 00:35:50,683
I've been asked to join as part of the audit team.

543
00:35:50,683 --> 00:35:53,752
You mean one sales team is auditing another?

544
00:35:53,752 --> 00:35:54,920
Yes.

545
00:35:54,920 --> 00:35:57,612
The pushback is gonna be intense.

546
00:35:57,612 --> 00:35:59,516
You expect that, right?

547
00:35:59,516 --> 00:36:00,916
Of course.

548
00:36:00,916 --> 00:36:03,160
Well, if you're okay with it,

549
00:36:03,160 --> 00:36:06,483
I'd like you to work with me. What do you think?

550
00:36:12,448 --> 00:36:16,496
Did you know I like Gi Tae even more after what happened?

551
00:36:16,496 --> 00:36:18,516
Because he ran around trying to fix it himself?

552
00:36:18,516 --> 00:36:21,816
Yes. He tried to solve it himself somehow.

553
00:36:21,816 --> 00:36:23,849
I'm like that too,

554
00:36:23,849 --> 00:36:26,516
so I like seeing him take responsibility like that.

555
00:36:26,516 --> 00:36:27,949
That's admirable.

556
00:36:27,949 --> 00:36:29,649
But still,

557
00:36:30,440 --> 00:36:35,172
ever since I became a team leader, I've been given things I can't handle alone.

558
00:36:35,172 --> 00:36:38,983
I boldly said I'd take responsibility for the Laknes situation,

559
00:36:38,983 --> 00:36:42,188
but Mr. Yang was actually the one who solved it.

560
00:36:42,188 --> 00:36:45,449
I can't handle this one alone either.

561
00:36:45,449 --> 00:36:47,683
I need your help, Ms. Jang.

562
00:36:50,524 --> 00:36:52,316
Why do you think

563
00:36:53,220 --> 00:36:56,768
I came back from China, Mr. Gong?

564
00:36:56,768 --> 00:36:59,249
Don't you think I'm involved in some kind of misconduct?

565
00:36:59,249 --> 00:37:02,316
I don't think you're completely unrelated to it.

566
00:37:03,249 --> 00:37:06,583
Then how could I possibly join an audit team?

567
00:37:08,636 --> 00:37:11,049
Are you involved in the misconduct?

568
00:37:15,164 --> 00:37:18,432
I assume you have a confidentiality penalty clause.

569
00:37:18,432 --> 00:37:21,416
Then you can just listen.

570
00:37:21,416 --> 00:37:25,583
I don't think you're directly involved in the misconduct.

571
00:37:25,583 --> 00:37:28,144
But you must be connected to it somehow.

572
00:37:28,144 --> 00:37:31,164
Whether willingly or not, you may have played some role.

573
00:37:31,164 --> 00:37:33,512
And I think you're keeping quiet

574
00:37:33,512 --> 00:37:36,016
out of respect for your colleagues.

575
00:37:37,716 --> 00:37:40,149
So here's my conclusion.

576
00:37:40,983 --> 00:37:43,183
You're the whistleblower, aren't you?

577
00:37:49,080 --> 00:37:54,183
I know you carry some guilt over reporting your colleague.

578
00:37:54,183 --> 00:37:56,801
And I've tried to imagine what you must've gone through

579
00:37:56,801 --> 00:37:58,783
after blowing the whistle.

580
00:37:59,780 --> 00:38:02,588
People must've whispered about you, and you couldn't say a word.

581
00:38:02,588 --> 00:38:06,283
You had no real way to explain yourself.

582
00:38:07,616 --> 00:38:12,316
Let people say whatever they're going to say.

583
00:38:12,316 --> 00:38:15,949
Why don't we just do what we can?

584
00:38:18,984 --> 00:38:21,504
Work with me on this audit.

585
00:38:21,504 --> 00:38:23,949
I'll carry some of that burden with you.

586
00:38:24,924 --> 00:38:28,028
Are you asking me to do this, so I can feel less burdened?

587
00:38:28,028 --> 00:38:31,688
No, that's not necessarily the case.

588
00:38:31,688 --> 00:38:34,020
They say you only know it once you've done it,

589
00:38:34,020 --> 00:38:37,516
so I figured you'd understand, since you've been there yourself.

590
00:39:02,016 --> 00:39:06,283
[2 Months Ago, China]

591
00:39:13,872 --> 00:39:15,856
Have you made up your mind?

592
00:39:15,856 --> 00:39:17,556
Yes.

593
00:39:22,249 --> 00:39:25,783
[Hongsung]

594
00:39:26,988 --> 00:39:28,716
Do you know

595
00:39:29,528 --> 00:39:33,676
what it means to be a whistleblower?

596
00:39:33,676 --> 00:39:35,252
I know exactly what it means.

597
00:39:35,252 --> 00:39:37,076
No,

598
00:39:37,076 --> 00:39:38,808
you have no clue.

599
00:39:38,808 --> 00:39:42,048
Not just in your work,

600
00:39:42,048 --> 00:39:46,044
you must live a completely spotless life. Got that?

601
00:39:46,044 --> 00:39:48,548
If you've ever dropped a single piece of trash on the street,

602
00:39:48,548 --> 00:39:52,456
people will use that to claim you're just as bad.

603
00:39:52,456 --> 00:39:56,640
Fine. Let's say you've never littered in your life.

604
00:39:56,640 --> 00:39:59,940
Do you think people are going to love you and call you a hero?

605
00:39:59,940 --> 00:40:01,483
No.

606
00:40:01,483 --> 00:40:03,436
Whatever the reason,

607
00:40:03,436 --> 00:40:06,604
people instinctively avoid anyone who's stabbed a colleague in the back.

608
00:40:06,604 --> 00:40:10,249
Especially in a small country like Korea, even more so!

609
00:40:10,872 --> 00:40:12,300
From now on,

610
00:40:12,300 --> 00:40:16,116
nobody will ever want to work with you.

611
00:40:16,116 --> 00:40:17,949
Just remember that.

612
00:40:20,416 --> 00:40:21,844
Did you really not know...

613
00:40:21,844 --> 00:40:25,116
No, did you really not know what we were doing?

614
00:40:25,116 --> 00:40:26,936
You knew, didn't you?

615
00:40:26,936 --> 00:40:28,908
Someone as sharp as you wouldn't have missed it.

616
00:40:28,908 --> 00:40:30,976
You just chose to look the other way.

617
00:40:30,976 --> 00:40:33,660
That's why we'd give you luxury goods when the time came.

618
00:40:33,660 --> 00:40:37,536
You knew we were even paying your housekeeper with company money.

619
00:40:37,536 --> 00:40:39,260
Yes, I knew.

620
00:40:39,260 --> 00:40:40,983
Then why!

621
00:40:43,700 --> 00:40:45,616
Then why?

622
00:40:45,616 --> 00:40:47,983
Why are you doing this?

623
00:40:49,392 --> 00:40:52,052
May I have a cigarette?

624
00:40:52,052 --> 00:40:53,748
What?

625
00:40:53,748 --> 00:40:55,749
Because I'm getting angry.

626
00:41:09,816 --> 00:41:12,449
Do you know why I'm angry now?

627
00:41:13,083 --> 00:41:15,783
You're using company business for personal gain

628
00:41:15,783 --> 00:41:19,504
and openly embezzling company money,

629
00:41:19,504 --> 00:41:22,660
and now you're asking me to explain why I'm exposing it?

630
00:41:22,660 --> 00:41:23,700
Wait...

631
00:41:23,700 --> 00:41:25,588
Does that make any sense?

632
00:41:25,588 --> 00:41:28,083
Of course, I've done plenty wrong myself.

633
00:41:28,083 --> 00:41:30,316
I've littered on the street before.

634
00:41:30,316 --> 00:41:34,716
And like you said, I did notice you trying to grease my palm

635
00:41:34,716 --> 00:41:36,356
with some of that embezzled money.

636
00:41:36,356 --> 00:41:39,116
So I tried to let it slide,

637
00:41:39,116 --> 00:41:41,183
but I just couldn't.

638
00:41:41,183 --> 00:41:43,949
I figured dragging it out would only make it harder.

639
00:41:46,416 --> 00:41:49,549
Why do you work, Department Head?

640
00:41:49,549 --> 00:41:51,216
For me,

641
00:41:51,216 --> 00:41:54,949
as I've gotten older, work is all I have.

642
00:41:54,949 --> 00:41:57,936
I don't have any hobbies, and I don't really exercise.

643
00:41:57,936 --> 00:42:00,168
But

644
00:42:00,168 --> 00:42:02,316
if the work I do is pathetic,

645
00:42:03,083 --> 00:42:05,349
then I become pathetic too, right?

646
00:42:07,708 --> 00:42:10,716
That's why I'm doing this. Because I don't want to be pathetic.

647
00:42:13,732 --> 00:42:15,583
I really need to quit smoking.
